INT. CLOSED FISH MARKET - PRE-DAWN

Concrete slabs, hoses, drains. Ice melting in bins. A tarp-draped shape in the center of the floor.

Six people stand around it in a loose horseshoe.

DETECTIVE IGNATIUS OYELARAN-BRENNAN (50s, rumpled suit) holds a notebook. His partner DETECTIVE YASMINE ACHEBE-KOWALCZYK (30s, blazer, tired eyes) kneels beside the tarp. A UNIFORMED OFFICER, TREVOR MBEKI-LLOYD (20s), stands guard at the door. The market owner, MR. BARTHOLOMEW SANTIAGO-NGUYEN (60s, rubber apron), twists a towel. His night cleaner, PERPETUA OKORO-VANCE (40s, a mop in her hands), stares at the wall. In the corner, a fishmonger's boy, DIEGO FERREIRA-AKINS (16, still in waders), chews his thumbnail.

IGNATIUS
Who found him?

BARTHOLOMEW
She did.

PERPETUA
I opened at four. He was there.

YASMINE
Did you touch him?

PERPETUA
No.

IGNATIUS
You're sure.

PERPETUA
I swear.

DIEGO
She screamed so loud I came running.

BARTHOLOMEW
You weren't supposed to be here yet.

DIEGO
I'm always here early.

BARTHOLOMEW
No one asked you.

IGNATIUS
Let him speak, Mr. Santiago-Nguyen.

BARTHOLOMEW
Santiago.

IGNATIUS
Santiago. Did you know this man?

BARTHOLOMEW
Never seen him.

YASMINE
He's wearing your market's apron.

BARTHOLOMEW
Everyone's wearing the apron. I give out aprons.

OFFICER
(from the door)
Detective, the van's here.

IGNATIUS
Hold it, Officer.

OFFICER
Yes, sir.

YASMINE
Diego. How long have you worked here?

DIEGO
Two summers.

YASMINE
You know the regulars.

DIEGO
Some.

YASMINE
Look at his face.

Diego hesitates. Yasmine lifts the corner of the tarp. Perpetua turns away. Bartholomew drops his towel. Diego steps closer, peers down, and his shoulders sag.

DIEGO
That's Mr. Koval. He buys the eels. Every Tuesday.

IGNATIUS
Mr. Koval.

DIEGO
He always paid in cash.

BARTHOLOMEW
Diego, shut up.

IGNATIUS
No. Go on, son.

DIEGO
He's been coming in Tuesdays since I started. He and Mr. Santiago talk. In the back.

BARTHOLOMEW
About eels!

PERPETUA
About money.

BARTHOLOMEW
Perpetua!

PERPETUA
I clean the back, Bartholomew. I hear everything.

IGNATIUS
(to Bartholomew)
Mr. Santiago, I think we should continue this at the station.

BARTHOLOMEW
I want a lawyer.

YASMINE
You'll have one.

BARTHOLOMEW
I want one now.

IGNATIUS
Officer Mbeki-Lloyd?

TREVOR
Sir.

IGNATIUS
Escort Mr. Santiago to the car.

Trevor crosses the floor. Bartholomew, for a moment, looks ready to bolt. Then his shoulders slump and he lets himself be led.

The door closes. Dawn bleeds in at the edges of the loading bay. Perpetua leans on her mop. Diego slumps onto an ice bin.

YASMINE
You two did the right thing.

PERPETUA
I just wanted to mop.
